<p>(all data in 000s except per share figures)</p>
<p>NOTES: Full company name is Washington Post Co.</p>
<p>Company says revenue and income increases resulted from strength in its print businesses.</p>
<p>Newspaper revs rose 8 percent in Q2 and first half.</p>
<p>Advertising volume at the Washington Post rose 5 percent in Q2 and 6 percent in first half from a year ago.</p>
<p>Daily and Sunday circulation of the Post dropped 2 percent and 1 percent, respectively, during the first half.</p>
<p>Newsprint expenses fell 20 percent in both Q2 and first half.</p>
<p>Broadcast revs rose 3 percent in Q2 and first half.</p>
<p>Cable TV revs rose 13 percent in Q2 and first half.</p>
<p>Newsweek magazine revs fell 2 percent in Q2 but have risen 3 percent through first half.</p>
<p>Revs from other businesses rose 19 percent in Q2 and 18 percent in first half.</p>
<p>Decline in equity earnings in affilitiates due to declining results at company's affiliated newsprint mills.</p>
<p>Company has repurchased 217,590 shares of class B common stock during first half at a cost of $75.5 million.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
